  "summary": "Serotyping and lineage assignment from sequence data are being automated and benchmarked against mixed-strain metagenome complexity.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is inferring typing-relevant genomic features directly from sequence-derived data, from cps operon sequences to population genome collections and metagenomic reads. ALLCAPS applies a deep-learning classifier for in silico pneumococcal serotyping, trained on 34,125 genomes and free of database or rule dependence. The Actinobacillus pleuropneumoniae analysis of 328 genomes links 23 lineages to K:O antigen and Apx toxin diversity. The E. coli metagenome benchmark shows gene content recovers well under mixed-strain conditions, whereas MLST and serotype assignments do not. The new element is explicit accuracy testing of typing under strain heterogeneity, delimiting where sequence-based typing is reliable. The items differ in method and organism, so this describes a dominant direction, not a shared algorithm.",
